### Reading from replicas

Replicas serve read traffic when [read/write splitting](/docs/products/databases/postgresql/connection-pooling#read-write-splitting) is enabled on the connection pooler. With `async` replication, a read that immediately follows a write can return stale data. Route reads that must see the latest write to the primary, or use `sync` replication.

### Limits and billing

- Up to 5 replicas per database; the maximum depends on your plan.
- Each replica runs on the same specification as the primary and is billed as an add-on. See [pricing](/pricing).
- Replicas live in the same region as the primary.

