#### 3. Store documents

A document's data is an `embeddings` vector and an optional `metadata` object.
The `embeddings` array length must equal the collection's `dimension`, and `metadata` is free-form JSON you can use to store any data you want to keep alongside the vector.

The vectors here are hardcoded so the example runs on its own. In an application, you generate them from your text with [embeddings](/docs/products/databases/vectorsdb/embeddings).

Use the `createDocument` method to store the embedding and its metadata.

